{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XSQohJaznweuGriUnqCUDZ","type":"tool_result","content":"- `new E.Input(screen, map, signal) → input`: signal: an AbortSignal that removes every listener this adds (game.dispose()). A screen without a canvas (headless) gets no DOM listeners: input comes from press(code), relea\n- `E.Input.DEFAULT { attack, dash, skill, jump }`: top-down / isometric action (Zelda, Diablo): Space dashes, J or click attacks\n- `E.Input.PLATFORMER { jump, attack, dash, skill }`: side-scrollers (Mario, Mega Man): Space / Z / K jump, X / J attack or shoot, Shift / C dash\n- `E.Input.SHMUP { fire, bomb }`: shoot-'em-ups (1942, Gradius): Space / Z / J fire (hold for autofire), X / K bomb\n- `E.Input.THIRDPERSON { sprint, jump, crouch, interact, attack, block, dodge, use, map }` †: third-person action and stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear): WASD / stick move, Shift sprint, Space jump and parkour, C cro\n- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SH\n- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n- `input.bindButtons(root)` †: wire every element with data-act=\"<action>\" inside root to the action\n- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n- `input.box()` †: the pointer's gestures, read each step in screen pixels (the HUD's space), from a mouse or one finger: box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; o\n- `input.buffered(a, win = .15)`: was it pressed within the last `win` seconds and not yet consumed? (input buffering)\n- `input.clear()`: Release all devices and discard buffered input on focus loss or a modal transition.\n- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null\n- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks th\n- `input.consume(a)`: mark a buffered press of action a as used, so buffered(a) is false until the next press\n- `input.consumeAll()`: forget every pending press (after closing a menu or dialog, so the same press does not also attack)\n- `input.doubleTap()` †: [x, y] the step a second tap or click lands within .35 s and 8 pixels of the first (a double tap), else null\n- `input.down(a)`: is the action held right now?\n- `input.drag()` †: how far the touch stick's finger moved since the last step, in screen pixels [dx, dy] (the HUD's space), or null while no finger holds it: to steer one to one (a shooter's ship follows the thumb) inst\n- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's m\n- `input.history` †: the last second of input, oldest first: [{ t (input.clock), dir (numpad 1-9 for a fighter facing right: 5 neutral), pressed: the actions pressed then, directions aside }], one entry each time the dir\n- `input.hold(a, on = true)`: hold an action down (on) or let it go (false), as its key would\n- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: in\n- `input.longPress()` †: [x, y] the step a press held still has been held .45 s (a long press), else null\n- `input.motion(digits, button, o = {})` †: a fighter's move in numpad notation, mirrored by facing: input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing: hero.facing, window }) is a quarter circle forward and punch (down, down-forwar\n- `input.mouseScreen()`: mouse position in projected screen pixels, or null\n- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n- `input.pan()` †: [dx, dy] how far a drag moved this step: one finger on open ground (not a box), or a mouse's middle or right button; else null. A free camera pans by it (game.cam.free)\n- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n- `input.press(code)`: press a key or button code ('KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:attack') as if the person did: scripted input, tests, bots\n912:  label(a, device = this.lastDevice) {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10afac7a-fac6-483a-81de-891e67f83b42","uuid":"713dfccc-b067-451c-b986-a32e34063d54","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:34:10.135Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `new E.Input(screen, map, signal) → input`: signal: an AbortSignal that removes every listener this adds (game.dispose()). A screen without a canvas (headless) gets no DOM listeners: input comes from press(code), relea\n- `E.Input.DEFAULT { attack, dash, skill, jump }`: top-down / isometric action (Zelda, Diablo): Space dashes, J or click attacks\n- `E.Input.PLATFORMER { jump, attack, dash, skill }`: side-scrollers (Mario, Mega Man): Space / Z / K jump, X / J attack or shoot, Shift / C dash\n- `E.Input.SHMUP { fire, bomb }`: shoot-'em-ups (1942, Gradius): Space / Z / J fire (hold for autofire), X / K bomb\n- `E.Input.THIRDPERSON { sprint, jump, crouch, interact, attack, block, dodge, use, map }` †: third-person action and stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear): WASD / stick move, Shift sprint, Space jump and parkour, C cro\n- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SH\n- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n- `input.bindButtons(root)` †: wire every element with data-act=\"<action>\" inside root to the action\n- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n- `input.box()` †: the pointer's gestures, read each step in screen pixels (the HUD's space), from a mouse or one finger: box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; o\n- `input.buffered(a, win = .15)`: was it pressed within the last `win` seconds and not yet consumed? (input buffering)\n- `input.clear()`: Release all devices and discard buffered input on focus loss or a modal transition.\n- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null\n- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks th\n- `input.consume(a)`: mark a buffered press of action a as used, so buffered(a) is false until the next press\n- `input.consumeAll()`: forget every pending press (after closing a menu or dialog, so the same press does not also attack)\n- `input.doubleTap()` †: [x, y] the step a second tap or click lands within .35 s and 8 pixels of the first (a double tap), else null\n- `input.down(a)`: is the action held right now?\n- `input.drag()` †: how far the touch stick's finger moved since the last step, in screen pixels [dx, dy] (the HUD's space), or null while no finger holds it: to steer one to one (a shooter's ship follows the thumb) inst\n- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's m\n- `input.history` †: the last second of input, oldest first: [{ t (input.clock), dir (numpad 1-9 for a fighter facing right: 5 neutral), pressed: the actions pressed then, directions aside }], one entry each time the dir\n- `input.hold(a, on = true)`: hold an action down (on) or let it go (false), as its key would\n- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: in\n- `input.longPress()` †: [x, y] the step a press held still has been held .45 s (a long press), else null\n- `input.motion(digits, button, o = {})` †: a fighter's move in numpad notation, mirrored by facing: input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing: hero.facing, window }) is a quarter circle forward and punch (down, down-forwar\n- `input.mouseScreen()`: mouse position in projected screen pixels, or null\n- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n- `input.pan()` †: [dx, dy] how far a drag moved this step: one finger on open ground (not a box), or a mouse's middle or right button; else null. A free camera pans by it (game.cam.free)\n- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n- `input.press(code)`: press a key or button code ('KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:attack') as if the person did: scripted input, tests, bots\n912:  label(a, device = this.lastDevice) {","stderr":"","interrupted":fal